.TH SETUP\-KRYX 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
setup\-kryx \- interactive TUI installer for KryX Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup\-kryx
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setup\-kryx
is the interactive
.BR dialog (1)
TUI installer for KryX Linux (automatically falling back to a plain\-terminal
menu when
.B dialog
is unavailable).
It guides the user through choosing a target mountpoint, installation mode,
package profile
.RB ( minimal ,
.BR base ,
or
.BR devel ),
extra packages, hostname, timezone, and optional Ed25519 release signing key,
then delegates installation to
.BR setup (8)
and offers to enter the new system via
.BR setup\-chroot (8).
.PP
Two installation modes are supported:
.TP
.B online
Install KryX packages directly from the remote
.BR kpm (8)
binary repository
.RB ( kryx-linux/ports
.BR rolling\-x86_64 ).
.TP
.B hybrid
Install offline CRUX
.I core/
packages from mounted CRUX ISO media
.RI ( /media/crux/core )
via static
.B kpm \-\-root
and overlay KryX binary packages and configuration on top.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Force plain\-terminal interactive prompts instead of
.BR dialog (1).
.TP
.B \-\-root \fIdir\fR
Pre\-fill target root mountpoint (default:
.IR /mnt ).
.TP
.B \-\-iso\-dir \fIdir\fR
Pre\-fill CRUX ISO media directory for hybrid mode (default:
.IR /media/crux ).
.TP
.B \-\-repo \fIowner/repo\fR
Pre\-fill binary repository slug (default:
.BR kryx-linux/ports ).
.TP
.B \-\-tag \fItag\fR
Pre\-fill binary release tag (default:
.BR rolling\-x86_64 ).
.TP
.B \-\-kpm\-bin \fIpath\fR
Explicit path to the static
.B kpm
binary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
setup\-kryx
setup\-kryx \-\-root /mnt \-\-plain
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setup (8),
.BR setup\-chroot (8),
.BR setup\-repo (8),
.BR kpm (8)
